; The structured SSA computation IR: typed values, regions, the builder, the
; verifier, the printer and the reference interpreter. Pure OCaml: no native
; process API, no physical target, no tensor or graph type. It sees only
; [core], [err_trace], [expr] and [fmt], so source lowering and the Loop
; comparison bridge depend on it and never the reverse. See the SSA design
; and implementation plan in .ai/.
;
; Wrapped (default): consumers write [Ssa_ir.Ssa_builder].

(library
 (name ssa_ir)
 (libraries core err_trace expr fmt))
